# netsurf: text paints at the composed group opacity (patch 311)
# Generated 2026-10-20
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 309)
#
# WS-A probe (a), doc 22: Firefox paints <span style="opacity:0.5"> text at
# 50%; VitaBrowser painted text/borders/images opaque at partial opacity.
# The group-opacity machinery (patch 149) composed per-box opacity into
# g_group_opacity but only background fills consumed it, so an inline at
# opacity .5 painted its text at 100%. This patch threads the composed
# group opacity into text runs:
#  - plot_font_style_t gains an `opacity` field (plot_style_fixed,
#    PLOT_STYLE_SCALE = full; 0 = unset/opaque, the plot_style_t fixes223
#    convention). font_plot_style_from_css zeroes it; all positional
#    initializers (box_textarea, form, plot_style.c, page-info) carry the
#    new trailing field explicitly (-Werror=missing-field-initializers).
#  - redraw paints text with g_group_opacity: text_redraw (all inline
#    body text, incl. selection-highlight copies), the select-gadget
#    text, and the overflow-ellipsis style (html_redraw_text_box).
#  - the vita text plotter maps the font opacity to the fixes49 stipple
#    bucket and draws the glyphs with that alpha (GXM/vitasim blend it);
#    the trace TEXT line appends "OPAQUE <bucket>" for non-solid text so
#    the gate can assert it (solid pages stay byte-identical).
#  - replay.c's TEXT parser strips the trailing " OPAQUE <n>" token so
#    replay draws the run, not the token.
#
# Proof (focused, nsmonkey-style trace via the sim): pre-fix the
# CSS-opacity-group page's TEXT lines carry no OPAQUE token at all;
# post-fix: HALFMARK OPAQUE 2 (.5 -> 35-60%), OUTERMARK OPAQUE 3 (.7 ->
# 60-85%), NESTEDMARK OPAQUE 1 (.35 inside .7 = .245 -> 5-35%), SHOWNMARK
# solid (no token). Pixel proof on the sim snapshot: darkest text pixel
# SHOWNMARK 0, HALFMARK 127, OUTERMARK 64, NESTEDMARK 191 -- exactly the
# bucket alphas (255/128/191/64) blended over white.
#
# Scope notes (recorded, not changed here):
#  - Group composition dedups by shared computed style: two nested
#    elements with the IDENTICAL style object (e.g. two .half divs)
#    compose once (0.5, not 0.25). Pre-existing patch-149 semantics --
#    background fills behave identically -- so text now MATCHES fills.
#    Changing it would move fills too; a separate patch if wanted.
#  - Borders and images at partial opacity still paint opaque (same
#    doc-22 gap): borders would need the group factor multiplied into
#    redraw_border.c's style opacity plus bucket plumbing in the vita
#    line/polygon/rect-outline paths; images need an opacity channel on
#    the bitmap plot op (tinted texture path). Both follow-ups.
#
# Simulator only; the vita cross-build was not run (no vitaSDK on this VM).
# Device expectation is in Doc 10.
